      "semantic_origin": "pdf_text"
    },
    "depth": 0,
    "payload": {
      "content": "Syntactically, there may be any number of except clauses, but you can code else only\nif there is at least one except, and there can be only one else and one finally. Through\nPython 2.4, the finally clause must appear alone (without else or except); the try/\nfinally is really a different statement. As of Python 2.5, however, a finally can appear\nin the same statement as except and else (more on the ordering rules later in this chapter\nwhen we meet the unified try statement)."
    },
